{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (#5136) from a code generation pipeline for the go-unix-utils project. The specific task is to create `cmd/basename/main.go` implementing srd015-basename requirements R1.1-R1.4 (core path stripping in single-argument mode). The task title is \"[stitch] cmd/basename: core path stripping (srd015-basename R1.1-R1.4)\". Only ONE file needs to be created. No test file is required in this task.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementation of GNU `basename` utility\n   - Differential testing against Homebrew reference binary `gbasename`\n   - SIGPIPE handler pattern: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n   - Copyright header required: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n   - Import path for sys package: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys`\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max\n   - No git commands allowed (orchestrator handles git)\n   - Write all files before building; build once with `go build -o bin/basename ./cmd/basename/`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd015-basename.yaml` (READ)\n     - Contains the full SRD for basename utility\n     - R1 (Single-argument mode): R1.1 (strip directory prefix), R1.2 (optional suffix removal), R1.3 (strip trailing slashes), R1.4 (all-slashes → \"/\"), R1.5 (empty string → empty line)\n     - R2 (Multi-argument mode -a/--multiple): R2.1-R2.3\n     - R3 (Output formatting/exit codes): R3.1-R3.4\n     - R4 (Differential testing): R4.1-R4.3\n     - Non-goals: no pattern/glob suffix, no stdin, no encoding handling\n     - THIS TASK only covers R1.1-R1.4\n   \n   - `cmd/basename/main.go` (TO BE CREATED)\n     - Must implement: strip directory prefix (R1.1), optional suffix removal (R1.2), strip trailing slashes first (R1.3), all-slashes returns \"/\" (R1.4)\n     - Must call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main (design decision D1)\n     - Package main, binary output to bin/basename (design decision D2)\n\n   - Existing source code reviewed (inline in prompt):\n     - `pkg/sys/` - exports `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` function\n     - `pkg/format/` - various formatting utilities (not needed for this task)\n     - `pkg/testutils/` - differential testing harness (not directly used in main.go)\n     - `pkg/hashutil/`, `pkg/encutil/`, `pkg/sizeparse/` - other pkg utilities (not relevant)\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet; code has not been written.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand the full requirement set for basename\n   - Determined that only R1.1-R1.4 are in scope (single-argument mode core path stripping)\n   - R1.5 (empty string), R2.x (multi-argument -a/-s), R3.x (exit codes, -z), R4.x (testing) are NOT in this task's scope\n   - Need to implement basic argument handling for the binary to be functional even though R3.3 isn't explicitly scoped\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - One massive task description message containing: role definition, repository file listing, project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, source code, requirement states), execution constitution, go style constitution, task description with requirements R1-R4 mapping to srd015-basename R1.1-R1.4, constraints, shared protocols, package contracts\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" requesting a conversation summary\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/basename/main.go` implementing R1.1-R1.4\n   - Verify compilation with `go build -o bin/basename ./cmd/basename/`\n   - Verify with `go vet ./cmd/basename/...`\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just read the SRD file (`docs/sp